// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 15-function-semantics
// facility: rule.fn.closure [Closure-Call] writes-self; rule.control.flow-analysis "A closure call"; D-0239; D-0245; conf.move-closure-writing-capture-while-shared
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.aliasing-conflict (static)
//
// Calling a `move` closure that writes its capture borrows it exclusively
// (D-0239), so the call meets `s`, a live shared reference to it. The flow
// facts show `s` live on every path, so the conflict is rejected before the
// program runs (D-0245; the tools faulted at the call until then). Before
// D-0239 both calls ran, and `s` saw the closure's state change.

import std;

fn main()
{
    i32 n0 = 0;
    auto c = move [n0]() : i32
    {
        n0 = n0 + 1;
        n0
    };
    auto s = &c;
    printf("%v\n", c());
    printf("%v\n", (*s)());
}
